Z||000000||200mph fierogt||04-26-2001||10:56 PM||||How to remove an engine in detail, please.For dummies, I don`t want to<BR>screw up on my first time removing on engine. And it would be the only<BR>way i would learn if I do it my self.<P>I want to change 4 speed to 5 speed. Can anyone give me tips please.<BR>what do I have to do.||||reg||5
Z||000001||TheFiero64||04-27-2001||04:23 PM||||Welcome to the forum<P>The best method IMHO is to drop the cradle down. This method is in the Haynes & Chilton's Manuals. You should get one of those and it tells you how to take everything apart step by step.<P>Good Luck, Keep us posted.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||3
Z||000002||danny boy||04-28-2001||12:08 PM||||Follow the chiltons manual. after doing it enough times you'll find some shortcuts yourself.<BR>As for the tranny swap, you'll need everything from the five speed car. Shifter,cables,slave and master cyl.s.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PFF_sig_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
